                <pb facs="0212" n="206" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg206"/>

                <head>No. 1.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Stevens to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu, H. I.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic">January 18,
                            1893</hi></date>.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Via San Francisco, January
                            28</hi>. (Received January 28.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Events in Hawaii in the past few days have moved rapidly. An entire overthrow of
                    the Hawaiian monarchy and the establishment of a Provisional Government in the
                    interest of the whole people of the islands without the sacrifice of a single
                    life. The new government is in full possession of the islands and was promptly
                    recognized by all the diplomatic representatives. The four men of whom it is
                    composed are of high character, one of whom resigned his position as one of the
                    supreme judges to assume the place. Pull dispatches by the mail leaving Honolulu
                    to-day by special steamer.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Minister.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
